 ratings."]}, "overview": "This open Texas border-district seat leans Republican by about seven points, and the special election follows Rep. Tony Gonzales' resignation. Republican nominee Brandon Herrera, a gun-content creator, has out-raised Democrat Katy Padilla Stout overall, though she holds a slight cash-on-hand edge and the DCCC has added the district to its target list. Herrera has faced sustained coverage of crude and inflammatory remarks, including references to Nazis, drawing national attention and outside spending against him, while House Speaker Mike Johnson has nonetheless endorsed him.\n\nNearly every expert rater calls the race Likely or Lean Republican, with one outlier calling it a tossup. Prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a 40% chance. The forecast lands at a modest Republican edge, with wide uncertainty reflecting thin polling and the volatility of a special election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2359, "margin": -5.0}]}